# Who must approve a change to main. Branch protection: "Require review from Code Owners" and the required check
# separation-of-duties (scripts/approval_check.py: an owner other than the author or committers approves, on the
# current commit). The last matching line wins.
#
# Test bed: one account stands in for every team, so one approval covers all roles. In the bank, use teams:
#   AI platform        @<org>/ai-platform            pipelines, checks, templates, onboarding; each project's access
#                                                    to models and tools (project.yaml)
#   Use-case owner     @<org>/<project>-owners       the project's agents, tools and evaluations
# (Team owners need the check's token to read team membership: a GitHub App token, not the workflow token.)

*                                   @dreadnaught07

# Use-case owners: their agents, tools, evaluation sets and docs.
/projects/models-demo/              @dreadnaught07

# AI platform: what a project may use (models, capacity, tools), and the pipelines and checks themselves.
/projects/*/project.yaml            @dreadnaught07
/projects/platform-eval/            @dreadnaught07
/.github/                           @dreadnaught07
/scripts/                           @dreadnaught07
/onboarding/                        @dreadnaught07
/templates/                         @dreadnaught07
